// Keybindings shared by the repositories that use this tooling.
//
// Why this exists: the mypy editor extension re-checks when you type, when you
// save, or when a tracked setting changes - but NOT when a file changes on
// disk from outside the editor. Edits made by a formatter, sed or an agent tool
// therefore leave stale diagnostics in the Problems panel.
//
// Choosing this chord was hard to do reliably. VS Code's published shortcut
// page lists only the COMMON defaults, so "not listed" does not mean "free":
// Ctrl+Shift+Y was chosen once on that basis and turned out to be bound to
// "Debug: Toggle Debug Console". The default set could not be enumerated from
// a remote server, because the workbench bundle runs on the client.
//
// Ctrl+Shift+Alt+M is a four-key chord, which no VS Code default uses, so it
// is very unlikely to collide. If it ever does, change it here (this file is
// tracked, so the change is reviewable) and verify with:
//
//     Ctrl+K Ctrl+S   ->  search the chord
//
// A conflict shows up as a second entry bound to the same key.
[
  {
    "key": "ctrl+shift+alt+m",
    "command": "mypy-type-checker.restart",
    "when": "editorTextFocus || terminalFocus"
  },
  {
    "key": "cmd+shift+alt+m",
    "command": "mypy-type-checker.restart",
    "mac": "cmd+shift+alt+m",
    "when": "editorTextFocus || terminalFocus"
  }
]
